  <title>Process deposits</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>Accounting</gui><gui>Process deposits</gui></guiseq> lists
  every check received that has not been deposited.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>Under <gui>Cheques</gui>, check <gui>Deposit</gui> on each check
    going to the bank. The count and total are shown below.</p></item>
    <item><p>Under <gui>Cash</gui>, type any cash going in, and the cash
    account it comes <gui>from</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Under <gui>Deposit</gui>, choose the date it is deposited
    <gui>on</gui> and the bank account it goes <gui>in</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click <gui>Process &amp; close window</gui>, or <gui>Process
    &amp; new deposit</gui> to make another deposit slip.</p></item>
  </steps>

  <p>Until the deposit can be processed, a message says what is missing, for
  instance <gui>Bank account not selected</gui>. The deposit then shows as one
  amount in <link xref="bank_statement"/>, matching the bank's statement, and
  in <link xref="deposits_report"/>.</p>

</page>
